# G118 — Mp3 Player

*Pilot — real Innate syntax, v2 of the Rosetta spec. See `mp3-player.md`
for the v1 pattern commentary (prose insights carry forward unchanged).*

---

## Choreographic Case: Vault Music Library

[mp3-player @library @playlist
    IN ORDER TO
        play tracks from a loaded playlist in authorial or shuffled order
        advance when a track ends, honoring repeat and shuffle
        let the user skip forward, back, pause, resume, and toggle modes

    [mp3[load-playlist {library: @library, playlist: @playlist}]]
    [mp3[play]]

    until @stopped [
        at @every 100 ms
            [mp3[tick {ms: 100, library: @library}]]
            #now-playing
                track: @mp3:current-track-id
                state: @mp3:state
                position: @mp3:position-ms

        sync @ui-events {
            play    -> [mp3[play]]
            pause   -> [mp3[pause]]
            stop    -> [mp3[stop]]
            next    -> [mp3[next {library: @library}]]
            prev    -> [mp3[prev {library: @library}]]
            shuffle -> [mp3[set-shuffle {on: !@mp3:shuffle}]]
            repeat  -> [mp3[set-repeat {mode: @next-repeat-mode}]]
        }
    ]
]

---

## Verb Surface (resolver contract for `mp3`)

The `rosetta-resolver` binds `mp3` as a context with these verbs. Each
verb is a `[mp3[verb args]]` invocation; state lives in the resolver
instance across invocations.

[mp3
    new-library           {}                                  -> @library
    new-player            {}                                  -> @player
    library-add           {library, track}                    -> @library
    library-get           {library, id}                       -> @track-or-nil
    load-playlist         {player, playlist}                  -> @player
    play                  {player}                            -> @player
    pause                 {player}                            -> @player
    stop                  {player}                            -> @player
    tick                  {player, ms, library}               -> @player
    next                  {player, library}                   -> @player
    prev                  {player, library}                   -> @player
    set-shuffle           {player, on}                        -> @player
    set-repeat            {player, mode}                      -> @player
    current-track-id      {player}                            -> @track-id-or-nil
]

`@player:state`, `@player:shuffle`, `@player:current-track-id`,
`@player:position-ms`, `@player:history`, `@player:events` are
qualifier-style accessors resolving into the player's ambient state.

---

## Constraints expressed as `where` clauses

The prev-button three-second rule, shuffle-seed determinism, and
recency-respecting shuffle are naturally constraints, not branches:

[mp3[prev {player: @player}]
    where
        position-ms > 3000 means restart the current track
        and otherwise pop the history stack and jump to that track's
        current queue position
        and emit a track-changed event only if the track actually changed
]

[mp3[set-shuffle {player: @player, on: true}]
    where
        shuffle uses Fisher-Yates with the LCG seed already set on @player
        (default @player:shuffle-seed is 42)
        and the currently playing track must stay at queue position 0
        so playback does not skip on toggle
]

[mp3[compute-next {player: @player}]
    where
        repeat is "One"  means stay at the same queue position
        and repeat is "All" means wrap to (position + 1) mod length
        and repeat is "Off" means advance if a next track exists,
            otherwise transition to stopped
]

---

## Demo

[demo
    IN ORDER TO
        exercise the full mp3 verb surface against a small fixed library
        and observe state transitions via emission

    @lib <- [mp3[new-library]]
    [mp3[library-add {library: @lib, track: {id: 1, title: "Alpha",
         artist: "Various", duration-ms: 120000}}]]
    [mp3[library-add {library: @lib, track: {id: 2, title: "Beta",
         artist: "Various", duration-ms: 180000}}]]
    [mp3[library-add {library: @lib, track: {id: 3, title: "Gamma",
         artist: "Various", duration-ms: 150000}}]]
    [mp3[library-add {library: @lib, track: {id: 4, title: "Delta",
         artist: "Various", duration-ms: 200000}}]]

    @p <- [mp3[new-player]]
    [mp3[load-playlist {player: @p, playlist: {id: 1, title: "Mix",
          track-ids: [1, 2, 3, 4]}}]]
    [mp3[play {player: @p}]]
    -> @p:current-track-id, @p:state
    ;; -> 1, "Playing"

    [mp3[tick {player: @p, ms: 125000, library: @lib}]]
    -> @p:current-track-id, @p:position-ms
    ;; -> 2, 0     (advanced past Alpha's 120s)

    [mp3[set-repeat {player: @p, mode: "All"}]]
    [mp3[set-shuffle {player: @p, on: true}]]
    -> @p:queue-order
    ;; -> [4, 1, 3, 2]   (seed=42, track 2 swapped to position 0
    ;;                    because it was the current track pre-shuffle)
]
